# The parser of a string comes first.
# CHECK-LABEL: role=Parser
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function

# The parser of a row. No name of the type needs an escape, so no key is searched for one. Where the members leave the declared order, one bit of the instance says whether the run time
# has met undeclared members under this shape. Only then is it asked whether it has parsed these names before: the call stands in a block of its own and takes its operands where they lie.
# CHECK-LABEL: role=Parser
# CHECK-NOT: :JSONKeyHasEscapes
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[shapesOfRow]] = Load({{*}}Reads:AOTInstance_mutableFields, {{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isRowSeen]] = BitAnd(b@[[shapesOfRow]], {{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isRowSeen]], Terminal, {{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK: = Patchpoint({{*}}:ColdAny, {{*}}:ColdAny, {{*}}:ColdAny, resultConstraints{{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK-NOT: :JSONKeyHasEscapes
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function

# The parser of the list asks in front of its loop, behind the same bit: the run time appends the rows whose names it has parsed before, and the loop goes on where it stopped.
# CHECK-LABEL: role=Parser
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[shapesOfList]] = Load({{*}}Reads:AOTInstance_mutableFields, {{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isElementSeen]] = BitAnd(b@[[shapesOfList]], {{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isElementSeen]], Terminal, {{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[firstOfLoop]] = Phi(ReadsLocalState, {{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK: = Patchpoint({{*}}:ColdAny, {{*}}:ColdAny, {{*}}:ColdAny, resultConstraints{{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK-NEXT: Upsilon({{*}}, ^[[firstOfLoop]], WritesLocalState, {{*}}:JSONParseExtraMembers)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
